title: "DRMYN Studio: Repository-Native Continuity and Look-Specific Alias Governance for AI-Assisted Film Production"
type: software
version: "0.14.0-continuity-alias-checkpoint"
date-released: 2026-05-12
repository-code: "https://github.com/hknbb/drmyn-studio-public"
url: "https://github.com/hknbb/drmyn-studio-public/releases/tag/v0.14.0-continuity-alias-checkpoint"
abstract: >
  DRMYN Studio is a metadata-only, schema-validated, human-gated research
  software framework for AI-assisted movie development and movie production
  process design, documentation, validation, and reproducibility. This
  checkpoint (v0.14.0-continuity-alias-checkpoint) completes the PROD-LINE-14A
  through PROD-LINE-14H continuity governance layer: character identity anchors,
  look-variant records, scene-to-character-look maps, and a look-specific
  Kling/Omni element alias architecture with scene-to-alias resolver and
  operator hint report. The repository provides canonical source records,
  planning metadata, prompt governance, JSON schema validation (55+ schemas,
  draft 2020-12), human approval workflows, evidence records, and
  reproducibility infrastructure for AI-assisted film production processes.
  Generated media outputs are stored externally and referenced through
  metadata-only records. Demonstrated through the Closing Price AI-assisted
  film project.
